1
00:05:22,105 --> 00:05:28,105
In an age of darkness, one man will face the ultimate battle against evil.

2
00:10:44,210 --> 00:10:50,210
Black Death is a drama, history, horror film directed by Christopher Smith.

3
00:16:06,315 --> 00:16:12,315
As the plague decimates medieval Europe, rumours
circulate of a village immune from the plague.

4
00:21:28,421 --> 00:21:34,421
There is talk of a necromancer who leads the
village and is able to raise the dead.

5
00:26:50,526 --> 00:26:56,526
A fearsome knight joined by a cohort of soldiers and a young
monk are charged by the church to investigate.

6
00:32:12,631 --> 00:32:18,631
Their journey is filled with danger, but it's upon entering
the village that their true horror begins.

7
00:37:34,736 --> 00:37:40,736
Ulric, played by Sean Bean.

8
00:42:56,842 --> 00:43:02,842
Osmund, played by Eddie Redmayne.

9
00:48:18,947 --> 00:48:24,947
Langiva, played by Carice van Houten.

10
00:53:41,052 --> 00:53:47,052
Averill, played by Kimberley Nixon.

11
00:59:03,157 --> 00:59:09,157
Wolfstan, played by John Lynch.

12
01:04:25,263 --> 01:04:31,263
Hob, played by Tim McInnerny.

13
01:09:47,368 --> 01:09:53,368
Black Death is a 2010 action horror film directed by Christopher
Smith from an original screenplay by Dario Poloni.

14
01:15:09,473 --> 01:15:15,473
It stars Sean Bean, Eddie Redmayne and Carice van Houten.

15
01:20:31,578 --> 01:20:37,578
Despite not being credited as a writer, Smith made very significant changes
in the second half of the script, including a new ending.

16
01:25:53,684 --> 01:25:59,684
All the scenes of Black Death were shot in
chronological order, a rare occurrence.

17
01:31:15,789 --> 01:31:21,789
The film explores themes of witch, inquisition, monk, village, battlefield.

18
01:36:37,894 --> 01:36:43,894
The tone is dark and emotional.
